    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (78.06) and **Gunnar Henderson** (77.04). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Anderson, where his elite contact profile is bolstered by a 7% platoon lift. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** faces Perkins with a significant 10% park factor boost, making him our primary engine for R/HR/RBI production. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused depth in the outfield; **Jackson Merrill** (69.87) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.12) both carry strong scores against favorable SP_xERA matchups (4.67 and 4.50 respectively). **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) earns a spot at the top of the order against Ober; the high score is driven by his 10% leadoff order premium and the 19% boost derived from targeting Ober\u2019s soft expected ERA.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Wade Meckler** (28.48) on the bench. While his profile typically fits our need for elite sprint speed, the matchup against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez is a \"stay-away\" scenario. The 19% drag from facing an elite southpaw arm, combined with his placement at the bottom of the order, pushed his efficiency well below our 40.0 floor, making him a necessary exclusion to preserve our daily game caps. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Nasim Nunez** (54.38); while his score is marginal, his switch-hitting versatility and historical stolen base utility prevent him from being displaced by the current bench options.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's lineup. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (48.88) represents a potential pivot point; his score is significantly suppressed by a -15% penalty due to the platoon disadvantage against the lefty Gamboa. While he remains in the lineup for now, any shift in stadium conditions or late-breaking lineup changes could see him moved to the bench in favor of pinch-hit volatility. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains unavailable, leaving us to rely on the current active core to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category.",
